{
	title: 'Steering spares unsafe-to-stop calls; restart warns',
	spec: `Bash takes an optional unsafeToStop: true argument, described to the model only as: "Use when stopping halfway might leave broken state (e.g. disk partitioning, database migrations, server provisioning)." The description never says what the flag changes. The tool card shows the flag on the call as an italic "unsafe to stop" in the card's own title color, never error red; terminal and web match.

Steering (ordinary submission, send steer:true) changes as follows; task 8p holds the rest. A tool call that has not started never starts; its title status is "(canceled)". A running foreground call without the flag is stopped at once: its process group is killed and the call returns, even if a process it detached (setsid, a daemon) still holds its output; its title status is "(stopped, 50.2s)" and its partial output stays. A running call with the flag is never stopped by steering: it stays in the foreground, its title keeps its elapsed time, and the new message waits visibly in the inbox; when the call ends, the model gets the result and the message together and the turn goes on. Steering never moves a call to the background. Escape, closing the tab and quitting stop every call, flagged or not.

Canceled and stopped-by-steering calls are not failures: their status uses the muted color and the card has no red error text. The model still receives a tool result saying the call was canceled or stopped by a new user message. Red stays for real failures. The status sits where task wm0 puts exit status and duration: "(4s)" while running, "(exit 1, 3.2s)" when done, "(canceled)", "(stopped, 50.2s)". Terminal and web match.

Restart warning. When a flagged call runs in any session on the host, a restart that ends the host asks first: /restart host|both|all from any client (terminal, web, remote), and Ctrl-R in the terminal that runs the host. Ctrl-R in a client-only terminal restarts only that client, stops no tool call and never asks. The dialog is a common/modals.ts modal listing each flagged call (block link, title, elapsed time), with "Wait" selected by default and "Restart anyway". Wait or Escape dismisses it and nothing restarts.

Emergency-key exception: tasks/README.md (Emergency keys) records this as the only case where a modal may stand before Ctrl-R. The check is synchronous, within the host process. Ctrl-C and Ctrl-Z are unchanged; Ctrl-C still quits at once, dialog or not.`,
	status: 'done',
	notes: [
		"Part A mechanism: prompts.submit defers a steer while running.unsafe is set (a flagged bash call runs) by setting running.steered; the tool loop's finally then calls prompts.interrupt, so later calls in the batch see the steered abort and get canceled results. turns.stop clears steered, so Escape/close win. A submit after Escape interrupts at once (controller already aborted).",
		"Results carry interrupted: 'canceled' | 'stopped' (no isError); turnPolicy.stoppedBy marks a dispatched call stopped (see the next note). A steered provider round now also writes canceled results for its streamed calls instead of leaving replay to pair them. The web had no title status (wm0 was terminal-only); it now shows only the steering status in the header, muted.",
		"A call counts as stopped when a steer aborted it and it failed (any tool, any error wording) or carries bash's stop line, built from jobs.byMessage. Matching only that phrase left non-bash tools (read_url, google) red after a steer. Invariant: a call a steer aborted never shows red.",
		"Part B: running.unsafe holds { call, input, at }; restartGuard.flagged (host/commands/restart.ts) lists every flagged call on the host synchronously, its block id found in history (the call's tool_call record), title from toolDetails.headline. Elapsed time is frozen when the dialog opens; it does not tick.",
		"Restart anyway sends /restart <scope> anyway; the host honors anyway only from a human, so a model's restart always asks. restart-ask goes to the session's followers. A typed /restart both marks the client before the host answers, so restart-ask unmarks it and only Restart anyway marks it again (terminal and web).",
		"main.ts wraps terminal.restart, so /restart local and SIGUSR1 in the host's terminal ask exactly like Ctrl-R; restartProcess.run (the host command's delayed exit) skips the check. A peer runs no turns, so its flagged list is empty and it restarts at once. The 400-line limit put the client dialog logic in client/commands/restart.ts (ask), not app.ts.",
		'Invariant: a stop (steer, Escape, /kill) or timeout settles the bash call at once. jobs.exec used to wait for the output pipe to close, so a process that left the group (setsid --fork, a daemon) and inherited stdout kept a steered call running until it exited; the steer never reached the model. Now stop kills the group, destroys the pipe and resolves.'
	],
	needs: ['wm0'],
	foldInto: ['8p']
}
